      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pembroke was incorporated in 1712 after separating from Duxbury, and was named after Pembroke, Wales.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pembroke%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An iron furnace was established in Pembroke in 1702, making it one of the earliest industrial sites in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pembroke-ma.gov/1719/Discover-Pembroke",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Shipbuilding and box manufacturing drove Pembroke’s growth, with box factories producing shoe boxes for nearby shoe industry and crates for cranberry and poultry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
